# Tasks: Phase 2 UI Improvements & UX Polish

**Input**: Design documents from `speckit.specify` and `speckit.plan`
**Target Branch**: `phase2-ui-improvements` (`/home/pplupo/repos/webui2`)
**Prerequisites**: speckit.plan (required), speckit.specify (required)

## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story] Description`
- **[P]**: Can run in parallel (different files/modules, no direct dependencies)
- **[Story]**: Target user story / feature (US1: #51 Pre-fill Project & Assignee, US2: #77 Bulk Add Mode, US3: #47 Date & Time Pickers, US4: #74 & #22 Remember Sorting & Options)

---

## Phase 1: Setup & Foundational Prerequisites

**Purpose**: Baseline verification of branch and component entry points

- [ ] T001 Verify clean test environment and target components in `frontend/`.

---

## Phase 2: User Story 1 - Pre-fill Project & Assignee on New Task (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP

**Goal**: Automatically populate Project and Assignee in TaskDialog based on active view filters and user settings fallback (#51).
**Independent Test**: Filter by a project and assignee in the UI and open the New Task dialog; verify Project and Assignee are pre-filled. Clear filters and verify Assignee pre-fills from `settings.assigneeName`.

### Implementation Tasks
- [ ] T002 [P] [US1] Add `initialProject` and `initialAssignee` props to `frontend/components/TaskDialog.vue` and update form initialization to respect them with fallback to `store.state.settings.assigneeName`.
- [ ] T003 [US1] Update `frontend/pages/index.vue` to compute active project and assignee and pass them to `TaskDialog`.
- [ ] T004 [US1] Update `newTask` trigger in `frontend/components/TaskList.vue` to preserve active filter context.

---

## Phase 3: User Story 2 - Bulk Add (Brain Dump Mode) (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP

**Goal**: Support `Ctrl+Enter` / `Cmd+Enter` inside TaskDialog to save and immediately prepare the dialog for consecutive task entry (#77).
**Independent Test**: Open New Task dialog, fill Description and dates, press `Ctrl+Enter`; verify task is saved, Description/annotations are cleared, Project/Assignee are retained, and cursor refocuses on Description.

### Implementation Tasks
- [ ] T005 [US2] Implement `saveAndContinue` method in `frontend/components/TaskDialog.vue` to validate, dispatch task creation, retain Project/Assignee, reset other fields, and retain focus.
- [ ] T006 [US2] Add keyboard shortcut listener for `(e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey) && e.key === 'Enter'` in `frontend/components/TaskDialog.vue` to trigger `saveAndContinue`.

---

## Phase 4: User Story 3 - Date & Time Pickers for Task Dates (Priority: P2)

**Goal**: Add append-icon date and time picker menus to date inputs in TaskDialog while keeping text inputs operational (#47).
**Independent Test**: Open TaskDialog, click the calendar icon beside `due`, pick a date from the picker, and verify the formatted date string is populated into the field. Type `tomorrow` into `scheduled` directly and verify text entry works without obstruction.

### Implementation Tasks
- [ ] T007 [P] [US3] Create date/time picker menu popups (`v-menu` with `v-date-picker`) on `due`, `until`, `scheduled`, and `wait` fields in `frontend/components/TaskDialog.vue`.
- [ ] T008 [US3] Format selected dates from picker into `YYYY-MM-DD` and wire reactivity back to `formData`.

---

## Phase 5: User Story 4 - Remember Sorting Order & Frontend Preferences (Priority: P2)

**Goal**: Persist table sorting order, sort direction, and rows per page across page reloads via `localStorage` (#74, #22).
**Independent Test**: In TaskList view, change table sorting to Priority descending and items per page to 25. Refresh the browser; verify table options are restored from `localStorage`.

### Implementation Tasks
- [ ] T009 [P] [US4] Bind `:options.sync="tableOptions"` on `v-data-table` in `frontend/components/TaskList.vue`.
- [ ] T010 [US4] Add `localStorage` loading on mount and reactive watcher to save `tableOptions` (`sortBy`, `sortDesc`, `itemsPerPage`).

---

## Phase 6: Polish & Cross-Cutting Verification

**Purpose**: End-to-end integration and smoke verification across all updated components

- [ ] T011 Run frontend build and linter checks (`npm run build`).
- [ ] T012 Verify complete Phase 2 user journeys: pre-fill, bulk add loop, date pickers, and persistent sorting.

